#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""orbit — the effective world of *this* binary, as a dumpable/diffable object.

Not `env`. Not `ldd`. Not `which`. The name on PATH is a guise; the payload
that will actually run, the libraries *this copy* will load, the env vars the
image names, and the SIP/hardened-runtime filter that silently strips DYLD_*
are the orbit.
"""

